# NOTE: every path in this repository must stay ASCII-only.  git-archive --
# and therefore `meson dist` and GitHub's generated release tarballs -- writes
# a non-ASCII path as raw UTF-8 into the 100 byte ustar name field, with no pax
# "path" record and no "hdrcharset" attribute.  The tar.exe bundled with
# Windows then tries to transcode that name from the OEM code page to the ANSI
# code page, fails, and aborts the entire extraction with "Invalid empty
# pathname", so the tarball cannot be unpacked at all.  Fixtures that need a
# non-ASCII name are materialised at test time instead; see
# PKGCONF_TEST_UTF8_DIR in tests/test-runner.c.  If such a path ever has to be
# committed regardless, give it an `export-ignore` entry here so it is left out
# of the tarball, and make the test that uses it tolerate its absence.

tests/lib1/dos-lineendings.pc eol=crlf
tests/lib-sbom-files/*.json eol=lf
tests/lib-sbom-files/*.txt eol=lf
tests/lib-pccritic/*.pc eol=lf
